      "input": "Is it possible to buy a train ticket through Trip.com using American Express?",
      "expected": "payment",
      "answer": {
        "text": "Yes—Trip.com’s own payment guide (updated June 25, 2026) lists American Express alongside Visa, JCB and Mastercard, and provides an Amex option to check when booking a train there. That support is conditional: it depends on the specific checkout flow and your card issuer’s authorization, so the Amex option may not appear or may be declined for a given booking.\n\nImportant distinction: this is a Trip.com channel claim only. It does not show that 12306 accepts Amex directly. A 2021 Beijing government guide for the English 12306 channel listed Visa, Mastercard, JCB and Diners, with no Amex—but that is historical and its silence is not a ban on Amex via other channels. Verify the current 12306 checkout separately if you plan to buy there.\n\nSeparately, Shanghai’s metro bank-card tap-to-ride (extended to the rail network from June 28, 2025) does support American Express contactless cards, subject to card conditions: chip type and ODA capability, small-value PIN-free payment enabled, and sufficient balance or credit. That is direct gate entry, not ticket purchase or app binding.\n\nNo booking has been made. For live confirmation, check the Trip.com checkout page and your card issuer; ask station staff about any failed gate entry.",
